# Play starts the tuning graph over. BUT_playlog_Click, finding logreadmode false - a log paused or
# at its end, or none loaded - empties the graph's lists (list1 to list20) and takes tickStart
# again, the clock its seconds count from, before it plays; finding it true, a log playing, it
# pauses and leaves the graph alone. `GCSViews/FlightData.cs:558-596, 3804-3806`
#
# The graph samples while it shows, whatever page is up; its facts are how many samples it holds
# and the newest one's time on its clock in whole seconds. The Play/Pause pressed is the LOGS
# tab's Telemetry Logs page's, which is the flight screen's own.
#
# Plays the recorded copter flight, so it needs no vehicle. Run from the repository root:
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-playback-tuning.gui -- file:testdata/mavlink/autotest.tlog
#

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 8
expect fly.playback.playing true
# Hidden, it takes nothing.
expect tuning.samples 0
click tuning-show
expect tuning.visible true
# Two seconds of the log on it.
expect tuning.newest >= 2
expect tuning.samples > 10

click tab-logs
click logs-tab-tlogs
expect logs.page tlogs

# Pause: the graph keeps what it has.
click fly-playlog
expect fly.playback.playing false
expect tuning.newest >= 2

# Play: the graph starts again from nothing, its seconds from the press.
click fly-playlog
expect fly.playback.playing true
expect tuning.newest < 2
